-- title:
--   Carry classes of a reciprocity homomorphism equal (m|H'|)u
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a finite extension $M$ of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ inside a fixed algebraic closure, acted on by a finite commutative group $H$ through semiring automorphisms, faithfully and trivially on the image of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ (hypothesis `hH`), together with an action of $H$ on $M^\times$ compatible with the action on $M$ (`hcompat`). Let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ which is a base for $(M,H)$, i.e. $K \le M$ and an element of $M$ lies in $K$ exactly when it is fixed by all of $H$, and let $u \in H^2(H,M^\times)$ be a local fundamental class in the sense of `IsLocalFundamentalClass`: in every enlargement of $(M,H)$ by an unramified overlayer datum (a larger field, a group with normal subgroups recovering $M$ and $H$, a Frobenius lift and a uniformiser), the image of $u$ under the induced map on $H^2$ is the inflation of the class of the carry cocycle attached to the uniformiser. Let $Nn \trianglelefteq H$, $\varphi \in H$ and $\pi \in M^\times$ be such that $H/Nn$ is generated by the image of $\varphi$ (`hzp`); every $Nn$-fixed $x \in M$ with $\lVert x\rVert \le 1$ satisfies $\lVert \varphi\cdot x - x^{N}\rVert < 1$, where $N$ is the cardinality of the residue field of the valuation subring `Rw q K` of $K$ (`hfrob`); $\pi$ is fixed by $H$, has $\lVert \pi\rVert<1$, and has maximal norm among $Nn$-fixed elements of norm $<1$; and $h^{[H:Nn]} = 1$ for all $h \in H$ (`hexp`). Let $f \colon K^\times \to H$ be a group homomorphism such that $\lVert a\rVert = \lVert \pi\rVert^{k}$ implies $f(a) \equiv \varphi^{k} \bmod Nn$, and such that for every subgroup $H' \le H$ and every $a \in K^\times$ which is a norm in the sense that some $H'$-fixed $b \in M^\times$ has $\prod_{c \in H/H'} (\mathrm{out}\,c)\cdot b$ equal to the image of $a$ in $M^\times$, one has $f(a) \in H'$. Finally let $H' \trianglelefteq H$ with $H/H'$ generated by an element $t$ of finite order, let $a \in K^\times$ and $m \in \mathbb{N}$ with $f(a) \equiv t^{m} \bmod H'$, assume the image of $a$ in $M^\times$ is $H'$-invariant, and assume the carry $2$-cochain of $t$ at that invariant element — the function sending $(c_1,c_2)$ to the element if the cyclic logarithms of $c_1$ and $c_2$ to base $t$ sum to at least $\mathrm{ord}(t)$, and to $0$ otherwise — is a $2$-cocycle for $H/H'$ acting on the $H'$-invariants of $M^\times$. Then the inflation to $H$ of the class of this carry cocycle equals $(m \cdot |H'|)\cdot u$ in $H^2(H,M^\times)$.
--
--   This is Serre's characterisation of the local norm-residue (Artin) map in invariant form: a homomorphism $K^\times \to H$ with the Frobenius property on unramified valuations and the property of sending norms from intermediate fields into the corresponding subgroups computes, through the local fundamental class, every cyclic-quotient carry class. It is used in the Herbrand-type comparison [`M4aHerbrand.exists_mk_localArtin_eq_pow_and_infNatTrans_carryFun_eq_smul_of_enlargedLayer`](thm.html#M4aHerbrand.exists_mk_localArtin_eq_pow_and_infNatTrans_carryFun_eq_smul_of_enlargedLayer), which identifies local components of a globally constructed reciprocity map with local symbols.
